  "captured_at": "2026-10-18",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "Watch a video about Audit Logs (shows legacy UI)."
    },
    {
      "text": "Zscaler records the actions of every Internet & SaaS (ZIA) admin in the Zscaler Admin Console and the actions that occur through the cloud service APIs."
    },
    {
      "text": "Internet & SaaS audit logs provide the following benefits and enable you to:"
    },
    {
      "item": "View Internet & SaaS alterations made to the Zscaler Admin Console, such as PAC file modifications or URL Filtering policy alterations.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "View details on all the changes made by an administrator during a login session.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Use them frequently to demonstrate compliance with security policies.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Detect and investigate suspicious activity and track unauthorized access to the administrative user interface.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "If an admin account makes 5 unsuccessful attempts to log in within 1 minute, the account is locked out for 5 minutes and the failed attempts are recorded in the audit log. The audit logs are stored for up to 6 months."
    },
    {
      "heading": "About the Audit Logs Page",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "On the Audit Logs page for Internet & SaaS (Data Explorer > Audit Logs > Internet & SaaS), you can do the following:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Filter by time range, action, category, sub-category, interface, and result. You can add additional filters for each column in the table with the Add icon.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          146,
          149
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Search for an audit log by resource, admin ID, client IP, trace ID, or configuration changes. The search only shows results starting with or completely matching the search string.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "Download a CSV file. The times in the CSV file are in PDT.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "Choose which columns display in the table.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4
    },
    {
      "item": "View a list of actions that have occurred. For each action, you can see:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 5
    },
